From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tom <tompt@seznam.cz>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:17:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: apple_tristar_charger: Reject an out-of-range
 battery capacity

A successful capacity read outside 0..100 was taken as the pack's state of
charge. Treat it as a failed battery read (-ERANGE), so the charger holds
and looks again as for any other failed read, on every board.

[Orchard: from OrchardLinux/orchard#205 (tompta1, 09038adf),
 kernel/patches/drivers/power/0050; commit message without the D2355
 charging policy it was written for.]

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
index e6ec63443..1917f0978 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
@@ -312,6 +312,8 @@ static int tristar_read_pack(struct tristar_pack *pack)
 		ret = -ENODEV;
 	if (!ret)
 		ret = power_supply_get_property(battery, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CAPACITY, &val);
+	if (!ret && (val.intval < 0 || val.intval > 100))
+		ret = -ERANGE;
 	if (!ret) {
 		pack->capacity = val.intval;
 		ret = power_supply_get_property(battery, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TEMP, &val);
